    "result_text": "There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the others are helper base classes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `capacityWarning` derived read field on owners. When an owner's city already holds **40\u201349 owners** (inclusive), `capacityWarning` is now `true`, signalling the city is approaching the per-city capacity limit of 50. The hard rejection at 50 (HTTP 409 in `addOwner`) is untouched.\n\nChanges (three files, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` read-only boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets `get/setCapacityWarning`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct leaves it for the controller to set (same as `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `toOwnerDtoWithDerived(...)` set the flag via a new `isApproachingCapacity(city)` helper that returns `countOwnersByCity(city)` in `[40, 49]`. This populates the field on both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nTest results:\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` \u2014 **passes**\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`",
