    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure and mirrors the established `bulkSignupWarning` precedent at every layer:\n\n- `isApproachingCapacity(String city)` is a private predicate sitting right next to its sibling `isBulkSignup(...)`, with the same shape (delegate the count to `clinicService`, return a boolean) and a matching Javadoc that even cross-links the hard-rejection path. This is the right unit \u2014 a small derived-field helper on the controller, not leaked into the entity or mapper.\n- Population goes through the single `toOwnerDtoWithDerived(...)` funnel alongside `householdSize` and `bulkSignupWarning`, so both `getOwner` and `addOwner` (including the idempotent-replay path) get the field consistently, with no duplicated wiring at each call site.\n- The mapper `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` follows the exact convention used for `bulkSignupWarning`, correctly marking it as a controller-derived (not entity-stored) field.\n- The OpenAPI addition parallels the neighboring `readOnly` boolean warning fields in placement, style, and description.\n\nNo duplication of the `>= 50` hard-limit logic \u2014 the rejection in `addOwner` and the warning predicate are deliberately distinct concerns that happen to share the same count source, which is appropriate. No class or method is becoming a catch-all. A maintainer would find this entirely natural.",
